{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe","id":1448799,"title":"Considering a Mongolian Tribe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-17T13:18:43-07:00","id":1448799,"title":"Considering a Mongolian Tribe","content":"Mongolia has a rich cultural mythology (a term I in no way mean to use to suggest &quot;falsehood&quot;) around wolves, and a relatively stable wolf population thanks to the cultural respect they are afforded. There's obviously a lot of cultural archetypes to draw on in the fashion that other Tribes do their associated cultures (for better or worse), and I'm considering either adding a new tribe, completely rewriting the Stargazers, or having a major branch of an existent Tribe (like the Hakken are to the Shadow Lords) help fill that setting niche.<br /> <br /> I would love to hear thoughts on what you'd like to see in such a Tribe or branch that both draws on Mongolian history, culture, and legend, without falling into harmful stereotypes (*tries to not eye the Fianna*). Would you rather see a Silver Fang &quot;House&quot;, a rewrite of the Stargazers, or a whole new Tribe? As Mongolian tradition sees wolves as messengers of Tengri, is there room in Werewolf cosmology for a Tribe with a masculine view, or even masculine counterpart (since Tengrism also features an Earth Mother), of what the other Tribes call Gaia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T13:51:26-07:00","id":1448801,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think there be connected to the Silver Fangs by sheer location? Maybe Siberakh.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the moon while considered feminine in Anglo culture is considered quite masculine in others like the Inuits, so maybe different Garou can think of Luna and a Women and others as a man.<br /> And the idea of a earth mother does exist in Mongolian culture and femininity is associated with deer.<br /> <br /> I guess a whole tribe of Mongolian-Turkic /Siberian werewolves seems nice and helps balance like the 5 European tribes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 05-17-2021, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T14:47:26-07:00","id":1448808,"title":"","content":"I've thought of the Silver Fangs as the tribe that belongs to the taiga, and the Shadow Lords as the tribe that belong to the steppe. Garou who live in grasslands don't have much to shelter them from a storm, so it's natural for them to appease Thunder. In my chronicles, the Shadow Lords are the main tribe in Mongolia and Central Asia. (Not the only one, as I don't hold any large territory is the sole protectorate of one tribe.) So all sorts of steppe peoples have had Shadow Lord relations regardless whether they spoke Indo-European, Turkic, Mongolic, or other languages.<br /> <br /> I think it's been a mistake of the game to too heavily concentrate on the human cultures of the Garou tribes' kinfolk as their tribal identity. While homids will have some of that passed to them, it would mean nothing to lupus. And of course, go far enough into the past, and there is no Mongolian culture. It's some other human culture, and before them a different human culture. What should be identifiable as a tribal culture/identity is derived from the tribal totem spirit which will persist as human cultures change.<br /> <br /> That's why in my games, I would have no problem for there to be a splinter branch of Fianna in Mongolia because why couldn't there be Children of Stag elsewhere? Their bastion of power might be Western Europe, but why couldn't there be a smaller redoubt that was established in 10,000 BC and somehow managed to hold on. They would still have lots in common with the Fianna of western Europe, but their homids would obviously be derived from Mongolian stock and culture. &quot;Fianna&quot; after all just means a warrior band, and all the steppe people's have those.<br /> <br /> And of course the Black Furies could also very well be in Mongolia as well, since the Eurasian Steppe is where the Greeks placed most of the Amazons. There's likely a few other tribes who could be located there as well that would make sense.<br /> <br /> Terms like &quot;Gaia&quot; are an artifact of it being an RPG. People should not get held up on it. Developers just ransacked their dictionaries and thesauruses looking for semi-appropriate, but unfamiliar terms to include as game terms to allow players to communicate to one another. They weren't scholars like Tolkien or Barker who invent a whole new language. The Garou Tongue likely does not actually use &quot;Gaia&quot;, and all the tribes likely use their human language for an appropriate term for the Earth Mother in order to fit in. But to make things easier for the players, we just use Gaia. As opposed to some made up term for it, or have these people use Jord, Nerthus, Cybele, or whatever. That just gets too confusing - players need a common language for common concepts. Likewise, the Get of Fenris consider Luna to be female even though actual Germanic culture considers the moon to be masculine. Garou culture and human culture are different.<br /> <br /> Cool things can be added to the game through exploring a particular folklore, culture, and mythology. But it all needs to be transformed into something the Garou would understand, and quite often that is different from a human experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T15:54:26-07:00","id":1448813,"title":"","content":"In my particular head-canon the original Tribe of Central Asia would eventually become Middle Brother after leaving and all that (which isn't official canon, but the three Tribes that moved to the Americas were all originally Asia Tribes even if where isn't solidly specified). <br /> <br /> One thing you can do with this, is actually have the Shadow Lords start as an east Asian Tribe, that moved through Central Asia after Middle Brother left, following the western spread along the steppes; with their eventually association with the Caucus range area being the western extent of the early Turkic expansions. This also expands the relationship between the Silver Fangs (who took over Younger Brother's northern territories, and Older brother's southern territories) as to the origins of the high levels of animosity between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T17:46:20-07:00","id":1448821,"title":"","content":"Yeah I guess worship of a deer mother is in-line with Mongolian culture. Could it be a separate totem then Stag do? I think Stag is seen as pretty masculine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T18:44:50-07:00","id":1448824,"title":"","content":"Steppe Striders are Canon but the only ever got one mention.<br /> <br /> Owl is well regarded as a protector against evil spirits across Central Asia, so I could see them being what the Hakken are to the Shadowlords for the striders.<br /> <br /> Of course in the region are also Scarlet/Red Talons, Siberakh, Stargazers, scattered Gonren/Wang Tong ( though with a different and better translated name ) and remnant populations of The Three Brothers kin who may or may not have been absorbed into other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T08:27:02-07:00","id":1448866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe?p=1448824#post1448824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steppe Striders are Canon but the only ever got one mention.<br /> <br /> Owl is well regarded as a protector against evil spirits across Central Asia, so I could see them being what the Hakken are to the Shadowlords for the striders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely wish the books had expanded on this more. I always think about it when listening to The Hu.<br /> <br /> I really like Heavy Arms' take as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T15:19:24-07:00","id":1448901,"title":"","content":"Right now I\u2019m leaning toward Clan Golden Sky of Silver Fangs being the dominant Garou of the steppes, and during the 13th Century you had a Garou war against the Beast Courts including Clan Golden Sky, Steppe Striders, Stargazers, and some Bone Gnawers and Red Talons. The Hakken and the Boli Zhousize sided with the Beast Courts, though thr BZ adapted quickly and well to the Khanate when it turned out not to be the \u201ccrush the cities and return humanity to pastoralism campaign they feared\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T15:54:45-07:00","id":1448907,"title":"","content":"My first impulse is to say &quot;but aren't they shadowlords?&quot; I don't know there's something about the Shadow Lords as being the Step people who keep testing the world riding in and rebooting things that feels so appropriate there. They aren't just Mongols they are every people who cycles through... the cycle of the step nomad who changes everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T16:07:35-07:00","id":1448908,"title":"","content":"That's why I mentioned the Turks, but the Huns as well. It's a great bridge between the western and eastern parts of the Tribe, and fits in so many ways.<br /> <br /> Attila's Shadow Lord backed army challenging the remains of House Conquering Claw sensing the waning power of the Roman Empire is really hard to pass up as part of expanding Garou history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:54:41-07:00","id":1448923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe?p=1448901#post1448901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now I\u2019m leaning toward Clan Golden Sky of Silver Fangs being the dominant Garou of the steppes, and during the 13th Century you had a Garou war against the Beast Courts including Clan Golden Sky, Steppe Striders, Stargazers, and some Bone Gnawers and Red Talons. The Hakken and the Boli Zhousize sided with the Beast Courts, though thr BZ adapted quickly and well to the Khanate when it turned out not to be the \u201ccrush the cities and return humanity to pastoralism campaign they feared\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: The most likely correct Romanization is Boli Zousizhe, as this was used originally in Caerns: Places of Power and Hengeyokai, and is an actual straightforward construction in Mandarin, even if it has connotations that weren't intended, literally being &quot;Glass Smugglers&quot;, with the characters for walking, secret, and &quot;people who do this thing&quot; (Boli remains untouched, and means glass). It got outright mangled in Revised, somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T20:31:59-07:00","id":1448932,"title":"","content":"Getting closer to canon, Clan Golden Sky was lost millennia ago, but their Mongolian kin, human and wolf alike, were claimed by other Central Asian Garou. The Shadow Lord who led the Garou in the Great Khan\u2019s hordes was marked by patters of gold fur in his black, and used his bloodline in his assertion of dominance over the Silver Fangs of Russia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T22:59:01-07:00","id":1448942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe?p=1448908#post1448908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I mentioned the Turks, but the Huns as well. It's a great bridge between the western and eastern parts of the Tribe, and fits in so many ways.<br /> <br /> Attila's Shadow Lord backed army challenging the remains of House Conquering Claw sensing the waning power of the Roman Empire is really hard to pass up as part of expanding Garou history.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view of the Steppe Garou and to a lesser extent maybe other changeing breeds is they are the storm. They thunder and lightning that destroys fields but also brings nations together. They are the storm that brings ideas from one side of the continent to the other. They force the weak to be strong. They force ideas that wouldn't work alone together. They take up the whole mythic view of history and make their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T00:44:22-07:00","id":1448949,"title":"","content":"In our chronicles Shadow Lords covers the altaic-turkic kin.<br /> Huns, Bulgars, Magyars, Mongols, Khazar and other ''ar''. For us in Mongolia, and among all the various turkic people, there are still packs of Shadow Lords.<br /> In many chronicles we create Shadow Lords septs and packs using ancient bulgarian or hunnic symbols and myths, some of them also get tribal names based on ancient hunnic names.<br /> This is also very historical-friendly regarding Wallachia, Moldova, Romania, and all the traditional territory of Grandfather Thunder's tribe.<br /> We are discussing about insert some ancient Wendigo awakened blood from the eurasian steppe to evolve the metaplot and make them less isolationists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 05-19-2021, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T09:32:44-07:00","id":1448995,"title":"","content":"Something I workshop for my own game the idea of kind of a sub-tribe that I go back and forth between titles like \u2018Wind Riders\u2019 or \u2018White Stallions\u2019 or whatever.<br /> <br /> I usually consider the Black Furies to be descended from the same ur-tribe that migrated westward from the Iranian plateau/caucuses area where they with Scythian and other nomadic tribes got settled into the Greek, Balkans, Turkey region. I usually have it that when the Black Furies became a tribe, the pre-tribal garou who would become the furies, with Luna-sent-Pegasus as their tribal patron. So the women and Garou-born who wanted would join the Black Furies and the men and the other Garou-born went elsewhere. Going eastward past the Iranian plateau I have them contact the Children of Gaia and with their stewardship effectively become a sub-tribe (kinda like the Siberakh) with Wind Horse as their patron (an abstraction of a figure from Tengri religion and parallel to Pegasus). This sub-tribe I have occupy around Central Asia and Mongolia with a heavy lean into the nomadic horse-rider archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T17:46:01-07:00","id":1449064,"title":"","content":"You mean Siberian peoples that are distantly reallted of the pure tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 05-19-2021, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T00:56:28-07:00","id":1449100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe?p=1449064#post1449064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean Siberian peoples that are distantly reallted of the pure tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno if you are quoting me about the wendigo thing.<br /> <br /> Basically we found a lot of references in 20th books where some wendigo are not native americans. We found african wendigo leading a caern in Botswana, kinfolk 20th says that &quot;Wendigo kin are theorically native american but exceptions always exist &quot; and Rage across the world &quot; wendigo almost Never accept anglos&quot;. <br /> We took inspiration from 20th MET book where it says that during the last decades ancient bloodline from Siberia and the russian steppe has awakened , and it cause some troubles among the most conservative in the tribe. <br /> <br /> So basically , the problem with this theory is that even if it sound really weird , wendigo bloodlines can awake even in some place in eurasia. We decided to use this plot to make them less isolationist and to evolve the metaplot a little bit from the revised. We really regard a little bit of &quot;genetic&quot; realism and instead of adding tribes we decided to make the already existing tribes more different without losing the sense of tragedy and tradition/progress that every tribe has. So, ugric/altaic ancestry? Yea wendigo could call you.<br /> Plus, in my party we are all italians and we Play here at the table: Its not about &quot;white washing&quot; the native tribe, its about the fact that we are ignorant about that culture and very far away. So instead of banning the tribe from play or risking to Play them in a dumb way, we created our own evolution and internal shifting.<br /> <br /> Now hate me if you want : mongolian wendigos who test themselves during winter cold night in the steppes, using altaic primitivism and ancient spiritualism to lead killer raids in Ulan Bator and other cities ? YES.<br /> <br /> Werewolf to me doesnt need more tribes. It just need more various concepts based on cultural and genetic history in order to not lost the identity of some iconic tribes but adding stereotypes and internal problems. <br /> <br /> Another example are the Fianna. There are a enormous list of celtic people and descendants. An english sept of fianna will be' totally different from a northern italian one, or from some fianna that can still be' present in Turkey because of the ancient Galati celts. The more european fianna would be' probably racist regarding turkish fianna, because thats it, xenophobia is part of tribalism , and I think its damn realistic and tragic especially in werewolf where you have to find balance between tradition and progress. &quot;Tribe&quot; for definition, is something primitive.<br /> <br /> Damn, thats what I want from werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 05-20-2021, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T04:48:42-07:00","id":1449103,"title":"","content":"Actually Native Americans where taken as slaves over the world, mostly the Caribbean but a few where sent to Europe amd Africa, that could be where they get the Pure tribes genes today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T16:21:34-07:00","id":1449291,"title":"","content":"Savage Age has the Tengger - which are proto- Stargazers + Three Brothers. They refuse to join the other canid shifters in the call to the War of Rage. The ones that displace themselves end up becoming the Three Brothers, the other part of the Tengger go into a sort-of hiding in the hinterlnd of Asia and eventually culturally evolve into the Stargazers. There is not much detail on them yet, but will be in the upcoming Player's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T07:43:13-07:00","id":1449342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448799-considering-a-mongolian-tribe?p=1449291#post1449291\" rel=\"nofollow\